# gate_state.json un-ignored (2026-08-29 audit, finding 29): it is the ONLY store
# MLGate._load_yesterday() reads for hysteresis, and being ignored it was never
# committed — every CI run started with no prior state, so the ±0.02 hysteresis
# band has never engaged in production. It holds only {date, status, threshold,
# spread, {ticker: bool}} — no private data; the same gate info is already in the
# committed latest_brief.json. run_manifest.json entry also removed here: it was
# tracked-but-ignored (committed anyway), so the entry was just dead/confusing.

